-- FTS5 keyword fallback retrieval over knowledge_chunks.text.
--
-- The FTS5 virtual table + sync triggers used to live here as
-- `CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE ... USING fts5`. SQLite builds without the fts5 module (e.g.
-- Android's system SQLite) fail that statement, and because SQLDelight emits `Schema.create()`
-- as one block, that failure used to take the whole schema down with it. The DDL now lives in
-- link.socket.ampere.db.fts.FtsSchema, installed as a separate guarded step after
-- `Schema.create()` returns, and the ranked query lives alongside it as a hand-written raw
-- query (link.socket.ampere.db.fts.searchKnowledgeChunksByText) since SQLDelight has nothing
-- to type-check `MATCH`/`rank` against once the virtual table isn't declared here. See
-- AMPR-325.

-- LIKE-based fallback for environments where FTS5 querying is unavailable
-- or for very short query strings that don't tokenize well.
searchChunksByTextLike:
SELECT * FROM knowledge_chunks
WHERE text LIKE '%' || :substring || '%'
LIMIT :limit;
